The 8th Commandment:


You shall not bear false witness against your neighbor!


If you attack one of your fellow human beings and strike him so that he is wounded, and perhaps even rob him, you know that you have harmed him and are subject to earthly punishment.


You do not yet consider that at the same time you are also caught up in the threads of a reciprocal effect that is not subject to arbitrary choice, but rather is triggered fairly, right down to the smallest stirrings of the soul that you do not even notice, for which you have no feeling at all!


And this interaction has no connection whatsoever with earthly punishment, but works quite independently and quietly on its own, but so inescapably for the human spirit that it can no longer find a place in all creation that can protect and hide it.


When you hear of such a brutal act of assault and violent injury, you are outraged. If people close to you suffer as a result, you are also shocked and horrified! But it doesn't bother you much if you hear now and then that an absent person is being put in a bad light by another through clever, malicious words, and often just through very expressive gestures, which suggest more than can be expressed in words.


But remember: A physical attack is much easier to repair than an attack on the soul, which suffers from undermining of reputation.


Therefore, avoid all highwaymen of bad repute as if they were gross murderers!


Because they are just as guilty and very often even worse! As little pity as they have for the souls they themselves persecute, just as little will a hand be offered to them in the afterlife to help them when they beg for it! The ominous urge within them to belittle others, often even strangers to them, is cold and merciless, and coldness and mercilessness will therefore be a hundredfold stronger towards them in that place that awaits them as soon as they have to leave their earthly bodies!


In the afterlife they remain outlawed and deeply despised, even by robbers and thieves; for a common malicious and despicable streak runs through the whole species, from a so-called coffee sister to the corrupt creatures who do not shy away from giving false testimony under self-imposed oath against a neighbor to whom they would have had reason to be thankful in many things!


Treat them like poisonous worms; they deserve nothing else.


Because the whole of humanity completely lacks the high, unified goal of entering the kingdom of God, they have nothing to say to one another when they are together in twos or threes, and so they cultivate talking about others as a beloved custom, the wretchedness of which they are no longer able to see, because the concept of it has been completely lost in constant practice.


They are to continue to sit together in the afterlife and worship their favorite theme until the time granted for the last opportunity for ascent, which might have brought them salvation, has passed and they are drawn into eternal decomposition, in which all coarse and subtle types of matter are purified from every poison that human spirits who are not worthy of retaining a name have brought into them!


(Abd-ru-shin: The Ten Commandments of God / The Lord's Prayer, Publisher of the Gralsbotschaft Foundation Stuttgart)

